  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PercentageOfWagesOfValueChainPartnersP5' (PercentageOfWagesOfValueChainPartnersP5) is '0.72' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PercentageOfWagesOfValueChainPartnersP5, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionsTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSignificantRisksOrConcernsArisingFromTheAssessmentsOfValueChainPartnerExplanatoryTextBlock' (DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionsTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSignificantRisksOrConcernsArisingFromTheAssessmentsOfValueChainPartnerExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Appropriate training and capacity building are conducted based on the concerns arising from the assessments. Additionally, HCLTech provides its vendors with an ESG manual and learning platform that outlines its sustainability objectives and expectations, including human rights.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DetailsOfAnyCorrectiveActionsTakenOrUnderwayToAddressSignificantRisksOrConcernsArisingFromTheAssessmentsOfValueChainPartnerExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NotesPrinciple5ExplanatoryTextBlock' (NotesPrinciple5ExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'E1 Employees and workers who have been provided training on human rights issues and policy(ies) of the Company\nNote: The entire personnel of HCLTech are categorized as ‘Employees' and not as ‘Workers'. Therefore, the information required in all sections in the ‘Workers' category is not applicable to HCLTech.\nNote: The above training is mandatory for all employees upon joining and must be completed on an annual basis. As the data is specific to the financial year 2024-25, the percentages provided do not account for employees whose training completion is due after March 31, 2025.\n\nE.2.\nNote: The entire personnel of HCLTech are categorized as ‘Employees' and not as ‘Workers'. Therefore, the information required in all sections in the ‘Workers' category is not applicable to HCLTech.\nNote: Disclosing gender is voluntary for HCLTech employees. The employees who have not disclosed their gender are categorized as ‘others’.\n\nE.3. Details of remuneration/salary/wages - \na. Median remuneration/wages: \nNotes: \n-\tUSD Exchange rate considered - $INR 82 = 1 USD \n-\tRemuneration of the CEO and Managing Director has been included in KMP information.\n-\tInformation regarding the Directors and KMPs who have either joined or resigned during the financial year is incomparable and has not been considered.\n-\tKMPs include the CEO and Managing Director, Chief Financial Officer and Company Secretary. However, the above information excludes the information related to the CFO as they received remuneration for part of the financial year.\n-\tThe remuneration/ salary/ wages for the unknown category is high as majority of these employees are based in Geographies/locations outside India. \n-\tThe entire personnel of HCLTech are categorized as ‘Employees' and not as ‘Workers'. Therefore, the information required in all sections in the ‘Workers' category is not applicable to HCLTech.\n\nE3.b. Gross wages paid to females:\nFor FY2024-25, the currency used is INR Crores, compared to USD million that we took for FY2023-24 data. For FY2024-25, we have taken the figures for actual wages paid this year, as recommened by SEBI circular (December 2024).\n\nE4 Focal point (Individual/ Committee) responsible for addressing human rights impacts or issues\nSrinivasan Govindan (srinivasangn@hcltech.com), Vice President – People Function, is responsible for addressing human rights related issues.\t\nEmployees are urged to report any issues pertaining to Human Rights to the Reporting Manager and/or the Global Ethics Helpline. Employees based in Germany/Netherlands can continue to raise their concerns and grievances by emailing to whistleblower@hcltech.com. \n\nE7 ii. Complaints filed under the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace:\nFor FY2024-25, based on SEBI's guidance, we have taken the average of females at the beginning of the year and end of the year. However, for FY2023-24, we have not changed the data. 51831 is the total females at the end of year FY2023-24. The average females for FY2023-24 is 60872.5. If the latter number is taken, then Complaints on POSH as a % of female employees/workers will change to 0.12%\n\nL4: Details on assessment of value chain partners:\nThe company’s assessment framework prioritizes risk considerations, focusing on business value. It emphasizes the inclusion of pertinent contractual clauses in both contractual agreements or Purchase Orders executed with vendors, thus, ensuring comprehensive communication of these requirements. New eligible vendors are assessed on these parameters as part of our Vendor Onboarding Assessment process.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NotesPrinciple5ExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
