  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DoesTheEntityHaveABusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlan' (DoesTheEntityHaveABusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlan) is 'Yes'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DoesTheEntityHaveABusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlan, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[As of 2025-03-31] Fact: The value for 'DisclosureWebLinkOfEntityAtWhichBusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlanIsPlaced' (DisclosureWebLinkOfEntityAtWhichBusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlanIsPlaced) is 'HCLTech has a robust business continuity plan. The detail of the business continuity plan is as follows:\nTechnological, geopolitical, societal, economic, and environmental risks are all coming together to create an intrinsically complex and fast-changing global risk landscape. \n\nThe Company's reputation as a 21st Century Enterprise is often measured by its resilience to threats, and how efficiently the Company responds to and manages business disruptions. HCLTech is committed to its employees, clients, and interested parties to ensure that necessary efforts are made to safeguard life and safety of personnel, protect property, and resume critical services at predefined levels in the event of any untoward incident. \n\nTo meet the organizational continuity objective, the Company has made significant efforts towards Crisis Management and Resilience planning to ensure effective response, prioritized recovery of its time-sensitive operations, and mitigation of potential business continuity risks.\n\nCrisis and Resilience (“C&R”) Program falls under the purview of Risk and Compliance function headed by the Chief Risk Officer of HCLTech. The C&R Program is guided by the Board, led by subject matter experts, and is based on ISO 22301 standard & global best practices. The Company undertakes active engagement with ecosystem partners for real-time horizon scanning of risks and early warning signals. The Company has embedded Resilience-by Design philosophy in the firm across different dimensions of the “new-normal” including resilience in work, personnel, workplace, technology, supply chain, and leadership. \n\nThe Company has started integrating climate change risks into each of these dimensions and their business continuity / contingency planning solutions.\nBeing an IT / ITeS provider, there is a potential that Company’s operations may be affected due to core-technical risks materializing in Company’s environment like technology failures, programming errors, cyberattacks etc. In order to mitigate these risks, the Company has embedded ‘Resilience-by-Design’ across the firm through:\n• Battle hardened Business Continuity & Disaster Recovery Plans including Cyber Incident readiness\n• Geographically dispersed Data Centers\n• Robust multi-vendor MPLS & Internet Network\n• Scalable Work from Home (WFH) Computing capability with stringent security controls\n\nHCLTech's Exercising and Testing Framework provides a comprehensive approach to validate effectiveness of the business continuity strategies implemented across the organization. The Company conducts exercises at facility, city, country level(s) based on nature, scale, and complexity of operations. Types of business continuity exercises include (1) Call Tree, (2) Tabletop and (3) Simulation.\n\nFurthermore, the Company’s Crisis Management Framework provides agile response, timely communication with internal and external stakeholders, and recovery & restoration based on the rapidly evolving global threat landscape, which includes climate threats.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DisclosureWebLinkOfEntityAtWhichBusinessContinuityAndDisasterManagementPlanIsPlaced, Context: ICYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'DiscloseAnySignificantAdverseImpactToTheEnvironmentArisingFromTheValueChainOfTheEntityWhatMitigationOrAdaptationMeasuresHaveBeenTakenByTheEntityInThisRegardExplanatoryTextBlock' (DiscloseAnySignificantAdverseImpactToTheEnvironmentArisingFromTheValueChainOfTheEntityWhatMitigationOrAdaptationMeasuresHaveBeenTakenByTheEntityInThisRegardExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Not Applicable.\n\nOur Request for Proposals (RFPs), at the vendor selection stage, incorporate ESG criteria to ensure that sustainability is a factor in supplier selection. Suppliers are evaluated based on their commitment to ESG standards, which helps us align our supply chain practices with our sustainability goals. We also employ a risk-based assessment approach to vendor onboarding which includes various aspects of the vendor operations, including adherence to ESG criteria along with pre-qualification on E&OHS (Environment & Occupational Health and Safety) parameters ensuring that the supplier meet our standards for sustainability and ethical practices. This helps the Company to proactively address the issues before onboarding the partner. As the risks are mitigated at source level, no significant adverse impact on environment associated with value chain of entity was identified'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: DiscloseAnySignificantAdverseImpactToTheEnvironmentArisingFromTheValueChainOfTheEntityWhatMitigationOrAdaptationMeasuresHaveBeenTakenByTheEntityInThisRegardExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'PercentageOfValueChainPartnersByValueOfBusinessDoneWithSuchPartnersThatWereAssessedForEnvironmentalImpacts' (PercentageOfValueChainPartnersByValueOfBusinessDoneWithSuchPartnersThatWereAssessedForEnvironmentalImpacts) is '0.72' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: PercentageOfValueChainPartnersByValueOfBusinessDoneWithSuchPartnersThatWereAssessedForEnvironmentalImpacts, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheListedEntity' (NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheListedEntity) is '0' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheListedEntity, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheTopTenValueChainPartners' (NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheTopTenValueChainPartners) is '0' xbrli:pure.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NumberOfGreenCreditsHaveBeenGeneratedOrProcuredByTheTopTenValueChainPartners, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'NotesPrinciple6ExplanatoryTextBlock' (NotesPrinciple6ExplanatoryTextBlock) is 'Essential Indicator 1. - Revenue from Operations in cells F11 and G11 is in INR million. And intensity is measured per million units.\n\nEssential Indicator 3. Provide details of the following disclosures related to water:\nNotes:\n- Data disclosed for FY 2024-25 covers India and global locations. However, FY 2023-24 data covers only India locations.\n- Revenue from operations has been adjusted for PPP using the World Bank's conversion factor for FY 2024-25. For FY 2023-24, it has been adjusted and restated using the World Bank's factor for FY 2023-24.\n- Intensity is measured per million units.\n\nEssential Indicator 5. - Revenue from Operations in cells F11 and G11 is in INR million. And intensity is measured per million units.\n\nEssential Indicator 7. - Revenue from Operations in cells F11 and G11 is in INR million. And intensity is measured per million units.\n\nLeadership Indicator 8. Green Credits\nHCLTech, through HCLFoundation, drives tree plantation activities. In total, we have planted over 3.2 million saplings. However, these tree plantation drives are not registered under the Green Credit Program. Hence, not applicable.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: NotesPrinciple6ExplanatoryTextBlock, Context: DCYMain)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Increased in Renewable Energy Consumption'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'As part of its long-term commitment to reducing its carbon footprint, the company has set a target to source 80% of its electricity from renewable sources—such as wind, solar, and hydro—by 2030. So far, 34.38% of the company’s global electricity needs have been met through renewable energy, amounting to 89,845.78 MWh. Of this, 58,263.35 MWh was consumed by facilities in India—including 2,615.55 MWh generated from onsite solar installations—and 31,582.43 MWh was utilised across global (Geo) locations.\nThis shift to cleaner energy has contributed to a total emissions reduction of 45,425.35 tCO₂e. Of this, 42,357.46 tCO₂e was reduced across Indian operations and 3,067.90 tCO₂e across Geo locations, underscoring the company’s progress toward decarbonising its energy consumption globally.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is 'This has enabled the Company to reduce carbon footprint by 45,425.35 tCO2e (Tons of Carbon dioxide equivalent) out of which 42,357.46 tCO2e in India and of 3,067.90 tCO2e in Geo locations'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives1)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'High Side: HVAC System Efficiency Improvement'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives2)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'By upgrading the chiller systems to magnetic chillers, enhancing control measures, retrofitting the cooling towers, replacing fills, and increasing the cooling tower approach activities, the company managed to save around 385.90 MWh of energy. This also helped cut down greenhouse gas emissions by approximately 280.55 tons of CO2 equivalent.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives2)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is 'Saved 385.90 MWh of energy and has helped to reduce 280.55 tCO2e of emissions.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives2)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives2)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Low Side: HVAC System Efficiency Improvement'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives3)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'The Company has made some upgrades to the low side of our HVAC systems across major facilities to boost efficiency. This included installing energy-saving units, upgrading to energy-efficient VRF and DX systems, replacing old belt-driven motors on AHUs with more efficient EC fans, and optimizing HVAC through activities like consolidating UPS systems. These changes helped the company save about 1,542.84 MWh of energy and cut down emissions by approximately 1121.65 tons of CO2 equivalent'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives3)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is 'Saved 1,542.84 MWh of energy and has helped to reduce 1121.65 tCO2e of emissions.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives3)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives3)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Technology Adoption'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives4)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'We've upgraded the AHU's conventional motors with more efficient EC fans, improved overall performance by using HVLS fans, and connected the AHU fan motors to VFDs for better control. Besides, we've optimized the cooling tower operations with SBR, which collectively saved around 443.66 MWh of energy and reduced CO2 emissions by about 322.54 tons of CO2 equivalent.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives4)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is '443.66 MWh of absolute energy consumption and has helped to reduce 322.54 tCO2e emissions.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives4)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives4)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Effective Utilization of UPS'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives5)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'Based on how much power the UPS systems need, we've upgraded to more energy-efficient units and fine-tuned the backup capacity by shutting down certain systems when they’re not needed. We've also added passive filters to help improve efficiency. These changes have led to saving about 1,268.48 MWh of energy and reducing CO2 emissions by around 922.19 tons of CO2 equivalent.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives5)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is '1,268.48 MWh and emission reduction of 922.19 tCO2e.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives5)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives5)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Energy Efficient Lighting Control'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives6)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'The company decided to ramp up its efforts to use more LED lighting across all its facilities—think workspaces, cafes, pantries, pathways, outdoor areas, and basements. We also added smart features like motion sensors and daylight harvesting to make sure the lights are only switched on when needed. These changes helped optimize lighting usage and cut down on energy waste. Overall, this saved about 123.53 MWh of energy, which also meant cutting down roughly 89.81 tons of CO2 equivalent emissions.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives6)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is '123.53 MWh of absolute energy consumption reduction, thereby reducing 89.81 tCO2e emissions'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives6)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives6)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Water Conservation'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives7)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'The company upped its water-saving efforts by making smart tweaks to reduce water flow. We combined Scale Bio removal with de-ionization in the cooling tower and also automated the garden sprinklers. All these changes added up to saving around 2.051 million liters of water'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives7)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is 'Enabled company to save 2.051 million liters of water'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives7)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative' (CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative) is 'None'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: CorrectiveActionTakenForInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives7)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'InitiativeUndertaken' (InitiativeUndertaken) is 'Transport Sustainability through Electric Vehicles'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: InitiativeUndertaken, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives8)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity' (WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity) is 'FY2023-24, the successful launch of electric vehicles (EVs) in Hyderabad and Bangalore marked a significant step towards our sustainability goals. By implementing long-term contracts for EV operations, the company has achieved a total emission reduction of 823.66 tCO2e compared to diesel-operated vehicles for FY2024-25.\na)\tHyderabad: Effective from August 1, 2023, we signed contracts with suppliers and began with 15Nos electric fleet vehicles. This number increased to 116Nos fleet vehicles, enabling us to perform 75% of daily trips using EVs by Mar’25. This initiative resulted in a reduction of 395.82 tCO2e emissions.\nb)\tBangalore: Effective from January 20, 2024, we signed a contract with our first supplier and began with 15Nos electric fleet vehicles. This number gradually increased to 90+ EVs, covering 75% of daily sedan trips by Mar’25. This initiative resulted in a reduction at Bangalore – Jigani of 422.56 tCO2e emissions. At Bangalore – ROB, EV operations started operating from 1st Dec’24 with 7 EV with existing supplier and reached 13 EV by Mar’25. This initiative resulted in a reduction at Bangalore – ROB of 5.29 tCO2e emissions. The overall reduction at Bangalore region of 427.84 tCO2e emissions.'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: WebLinkForDetailsOfInitiativeTakenByEntity, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives8)"
  },
  {
    "text": "[Unknown Period] Fact: The value for 'OutcomeOfTheInitiative' (OutcomeOfTheInitiative) is 'By implementing long-term contracts for EV operations, the company has achieved a total emission reduction of 823.66 tCO2e compared to diesel-operated vehicles for FY2024-25'.",
    "source": "XBRL Fact (Concept: OutcomeOfTheInitiative, Context: D_SpecificInitiatives8)"
